reprint</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b29\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Make it home: automatic optimization of furniture arrangement</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">L.-F</forename><surname>Yu</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">S.-K</forename><surname>Yeung</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">C.-K</forename><surname>Tang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">D</forename><surname>Terzopoulos</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">T</forename><forename type=\"middle\">F</forename><surname>Chan</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">S</forename><forename type=\"middle\">J</forename><surname>Osher</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<idno type=\"DOI\">10.1145/2010324.1964981</idno>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/2010324.1964981\" />\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"j\">ACM Trans. Graph</title>\n\t\t<idno type=\"ISSN\">0730-0301</idno>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"volume\">30</biblScope>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"issue\">4</biblScope>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2011-07\">July 2011</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b30\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Immersegen: Agent-guided immersive world generation with alpha-textured proxies</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">J</forename><surname>Yuan</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">B</forename><surname>Yang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">K</forename><surname>Wang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">P</forename><surname>Pan</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">L</forename><surname>Ma</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">X</forename><surname>Zhang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">X</forename><surname>Liu</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Z</forename><surname>Cui</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Y</forename><surname>Ma</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.14315\" />\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2025\">2025</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b31\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Language agent tree search unifies reasoning acting and planning in language models</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">A</forename><surname>Zhou</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">K</forename><surname>Yan</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">M</forename><surname>Shlapentokh-Rothman</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">H</forename><surname>Wang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Y.-X</forename><surname>Wang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.04406\" />\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">You are an expert 4D Dynamics Analyst for &quot;4DCoder</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2024\">2024</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Code2Worlds: Empowering Coding LLMs for 4D World Generation Your goal is to identify the SINGLE most critical &quot;Key Object&quot; from a scene description that requires dynamic simulation (physics, motion, or deformation</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b32\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">You must return a strictly formatted JSON Object (not a list</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">### Output</forename><surname>Format</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>with exactly two keys</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b33\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">A single, lowercase, common noun representing the object&apos;s category</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>No adjectives, no quantities</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b34\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">A brief explanation of why this object is the dynamic focal point</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b35\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title/>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">### Selection</forename><surname>Rules</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Priority Order</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b36\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Passive: Select the object moving, falling, breaking, or deforming</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Active vs Ignore static colliders (e.g., floor, table, wall</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b37\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">The &quot;Victim&quot; or &quot;Agent&quot;: If an object is being acted upon</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>e.g., &quot;can&quot; being crushed), it is the key object</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b38\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Prefer objects requiring simulation (Cloth, Soft Body, Fluid Emitter) over simple rigid translation</title>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"j\">Complexity</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b39\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title/>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">### Formatting</forename><surname>Rules</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b40\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Strict Noun Only: -BAD</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>red cup&quot;, &quot;shattering glass&quot;, &quot;a pair of shoes&quot;. -GOOD: &quot;cup&quot;, &quot;glass&quot;, &quot;shoe</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b41\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Singular Form: Always convert to singular</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>e.g., &quot;leaves</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b42\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">No Backgrounds: Never select</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>ground&quot;, &quot;floor&quot;, &quot;sky&quot;, or &quot;room</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b43\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">A heavy iron anvil crushing a soda can</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">### Examples:</forename><surname>User</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">The can is the object undergoing deformation (soft body physics), while the anvil is just a rigid collider</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Output: { &quot;key_obj&quot;: &quot;can</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b44\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Your task is to evaluate the RICHNESS and DIVERSITY of objects in the scene image. IMPORTANT: You should NOT consider whether the scene matches any text prompt</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>User</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Figure 22. Example of leaf Prompt Code2Worlds: Empowering Coding LLMs for 4D World Generation</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Output: { &quot;key_obj&quot;: &quot;leaf Thousands of golden maple leaves falling in the wind A glass of water spilling onto a wooden table Output: { &quot;key_obj&quot;: &quot;glass The leaves are the active dynamic elements controlled by wind forces You are a Scene Richness Evaluator for 3D environments The glass is the source of the fluid interaction and motion, whereas the table is a static passive collider Focus ONLY on the visual richness of what you see</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n\t\t\t\t</listBibl>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</back>\n\t</text>\n</TEI>\n","pdf_hash":"d3b3cf9537f35167af2725a7a6c58629b98bc7596ba9069d28e6712a05eb8fa6","tables":[{"table_id":"tab_0","section_path_id":"1~53","section_ordinal":67,"caption":"Table 1 .","coordinates":null,"cells":[{"row":0,"column":0,"colspan":5,"rowspan":1,"text":"Code2Worlds: Empowering Coding LLMs for 4D World Generation","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":467,"end":526},"digest":"44864a83777d86ba97b3015a65f9cb11b9365a7cfe184c8fa2c001e8a41594ba"},{"row":0,"column":5,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":526,"end":526},"digest":"eb71df8bab690d4fb0739206468d7b153927f36e2c66221a63e5a901a3018e45"},{"row":0,"column":6,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":526,"end":526},"digest":"996ab3fdbdb605a59046b5c21c10575d6be035de1bca30d202afe8a1218870fd"},{"row":1,"column":0,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"Method","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":526,"end":532},"digest":"47d67cf755170843dbdbeab7c3f740b14ddecd089e9a0ba7bfe37f03b6fbaad7"},{"row":1,"column":1,"colsp